      "text": "A, B Only",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to Fajan&#39;s Rule, small cation has more polarising power and larger anion has more polarisability. These&nbsp;small cations and larger anions favours covalent character.</p><p>A.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KF</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>KI</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math>False (Iodide is larger anion than&nbsp;fluoride)</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiF</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>KF</mi><mo>-</mo></math>True (Lithium-ion is smaller cation than potassium ion)</p><p>B.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KF</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>KI</mi><mo>-</mo></math>True;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiF</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>KF</mi><mo>-</mo></math>True</p><p>C.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SnCl</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>SnCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></math>True(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is smaller than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>);&nbsp;</p><p>The ions with pseudo inert gas configuration prefers the covalent character.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CuCl</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>NaCl</mi><mo>-</mo></math>True(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;ion has pseudo inert gas configuration)</p><p>D.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LiF</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>KF</mi><mo>-</mo></math>True;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CuCl</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>NaCl</mi><mo>-</mo></math>False</p><p>E.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KF</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>KI</mi><mo>-</mo></math>True;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CuCl</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>NaCl</mi><mo>-</mo></math>True</p>"
  }
